--TEST--
`static fn` and `extract` are the two rows of the functions, constants and scope table no other case refuses — `rule:statements/no-function-static-and-no-global`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:php-differences/the-short-list
// An anonymous function captures `$this` only if it uses it, so `static` in front of one
// is `E0210`. `extract` makes variables whose names are only known at run
// time, so it is `E0205`.
class Prices {
    public static function doubler(): callable {
        return static fn(int $a): int => $a * 2;
    }
}

array<int> $arr = ["a" => 1];
extract($arr);
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0210]: `static` is not allowed before an anonymous function
%A
error[E0205]: `extract` is not supported
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
